# PAM stack for kldload-install-kiosk.service (systemd PAMName=kldload-kiosk).
#
# Read by: pam_systemd, via systemd's PAM session setup for that unit.
# What it is for: registering a logind SESSION on seat0 for tty1, so cage can
# be handed the DRM and input devices as the unprivileged `live` user. That is
# the whole job — there is no password to check, because systemd runs only the
# account and session stacks of a PAMName= file, never auth.
#
# Consequence if missing: systemd cannot open the PAM session, the unit fails
# with a PAM error, and the install show never appears. A dedicated stack
# rather than reusing /etc/pam.d/login, because login's session stack pulls in
# pam_selinux and pam_keyinit, neither of which has anything to do with a
# kiosk — and the live image boots with selinux=0 on the cmdline anyway.
auth       required    pam_permit.so
account    required    pam_unix.so
session    required    pam_limits.so
session    required    pam_unix.so
session    optional    pam_loginuid.so
# The one that matters. After pam_loginuid, so the session is registered with
# the loginuid already set.
session    optional    pam_systemd.so
